      content:
        '# Mental Health Information\n\nhtml PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0 Transitional//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/loose.dtd"\n\nThe National Institute of Mental Health (NIMH) offers authoritative information about mental disorders, a range of related topics, and the latest mental health research.\n\n##### Featured Topics and Events\n\n[Suicide Prevention Month (September 2025)](https://www.nimh.nih.gov/get-involved/digital-shareables/shareable-resources-on-suicide-prevention)\n\nHelp raise awareness about suicide prevention. Download and share social media graphics and messages from NIMH to spread the word and promote understanding.\n\n##### [Health Topics](https://www.nimh.nih.gov/health/topics)\n\nLearn more about mental disorders, treatments and therapies, and where to find clinical trials.\n\n##### [Statistics](https://www.nimh.nih.gov/health/statistics)\n\nNIMH statistics pages include statistics on the prevalence, treatment, and costs of mental illness for the population of the United States, in addition to information about possible consequences of mental illnesses, such as suicide and disability.\n\n##### [Brochures and Fact Sheets](https://www.nimh.nih.gov/health/publications)\n\nDownload and read free digital NIMH brochures and fact sheets about mental disorders and related topics. Publications are also available in Spanish.\n\n##### [Help for Mental Illnesses](https://www.nimh.nih.gov/health/find-help)\n\nIf you or someone you know has a mental illness, there are ways to get help. Use these resources to find help for yourself, a friend, or a family member. ([Esta página también está disponible en español](https://www.nimh.nih.gov/health/find-help/ayuda-para-la-salud-mental).)\n\n##### [Clinical Trials](https://www.nimh.nih.gov/health/trials)\n\nLearn about clinical trials, why people participate in them, what to expect during one, how to find a study, and what to expect after the trial is done.\n\nUnless otherwise specified, NIMH information and publications are in the public domain and available for use free of charge. Citation of the NIMH is appreciated. Please see our [Citing NIMH Information and Publications](https://www.nimh.nih.gov/site-info/citing-nimh-publications-and-webpages) page for more information.',
